{"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Localization","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Overriding text per-app","anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}]},{"code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"text":", mirroring ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"text":" from the SwiftUI side.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateContainerView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScreenStateContainerView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewController"},{"text":" base class that owns a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pinned to the view’s edges and bound to a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screens